## Attribution Guidelines

### How to Attribute

When using this library in your project, attribution can be provided in one of the following ways:

**Option 1: In your package.json**
```json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "create-http-resources-slice": "^0.1.0"
  },
  "credits": "This project uses create-http-resources-slice (MIT License)"
}
```

**Option 2: In your README**
```markdown
## Credits
This project uses [create-http-resources-slice](https://github.com/yourusername/create-http-resources-slice) (MIT License).
```

**Option 3: In a NOTICE file**
```
This product includes create-http-resources-slice
Copyright (c) 2024 create-http-resources-slice
Licensed under MIT License
```

### When Attribution is Required

- ✅ Distributing the library (modified or unmodified)
- ✅ Creating derivative works based on this library
- ✅ Including this library in a larger software package
- ✅ Using this library in commercial products

### When Attribution is NOT Required

- ❌ Using the library as intended (normal import/usage in your application)
- ❌ Private/internal use without distribution

For questions about attribution requirements, please contact the maintainers.
